  "limits": [
    "Only the exhibited association/MAC peak is completed. No global termination, confluence, finite mixed homotopy basis, complete wire-equation presentation, or arbitrary-track coherence theorem is claimed.",
    "The finite schema has infinitely many typed instances. HigherBasis does not itself require a finite family. No arbitrary parallel-path comparison is made a generator.",
    "No forward join in the naive catalogue is not semantic inequality or absence of a reversible proof track. Formal inverse reverses an equality-preserving proof rewrite, never probabilistic execution.",
    "The candidate flag and candidate count over-approximate possible rewrites. Zero rules out steps; positivity does not certify an actual step.",
    "Dependency accounting is conservative and not a minimal-obligation or minimum-cost theorem. Its semantic consequence is kernel equality in the updated model, not equality between old and updated models or equality of arbitrary couplings.",
    "The existing actual MAC base kernels and conditions are retained, including full state and trace. No new security bound, attack/query order, computational reduction implementation, native continuing machine execution, or actual runtime result is proved here.",
    "Twelve constructors is a count of this constructed higher term only. No total serialized size, shared-DAG checking complexity, independent ordinary comparison, or dimension-exclusive advantage is established.",
    "The earlier RootRigid-based normalization cannot be applied to this enlarged catalogue. Further structural and mixed critical overlaps require separate work."
  ],
